## Verifying your work

Run before reporting a task complete and paste the output. Fix the code, never the check.

- `make check` (healthy output ends with `compose check passed` and no shellcheck findings)
- With a real instance file: `make check INSTANCE=<name>`

## Conventions

- Deploy-time values (ports, GPU UUIDs, data path, caps) live in `instances/<name>.env`, gitignored except `example.env`. Secrets live in `secrets/app.env` (gitignored, loaded via `env_file`).
- Ports bind to `127.0.0.1`; reach them with `ssh -L`.{% if kind == 'workspace' %} Only the SSH port (container 2222) may use another `BIND_ADDR`.{% endif %}
- GPUs: `runtime: nvidia` and `GPU_UUIDS` from `nvidia-smi -L`; never `all` or a GPU index.
- Images are tagged `<version>-<variant>`; never `latest`. Releases come from conventional commits on `main`.
- Persistent data goes to `/data` (`DATA_ROOT` on the large disk){% if kind == 'workspace' %} or the `home`/`tmp` volumes{% endif %}, never into the container writable layer.

## Architecture

{%- if kind == 'workspace' or build %}
- `.docker/Dockerfile`: one Dockerfile; `BASE_IMAGE` comes from `.docker/variants/<variant>.env`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if kind == 'workspace' %}
- `.docker/entrypoint.sh`, `.docker/sshd_config`: unprivileged key-only sshd; host key in `~/.workspace`.
{%- endif %}
- `compose.yaml`: the run spec. `scripts/check-compose.sh`: the rules `make check` enforces.
- `.github/workflows/`: `ci.yaml` (PR checks{% if kind == 'workspace' or build %} and builds without push{% endif %}), `release.yaml` (tag{% if kind == 'workspace' or build %}, then push images{% endif %}).

